    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** and **Yordan Alvarez** anchoring the offense, representing our most potent options with scores of 80.95 and 79.83, respectively. **Junior Caminero** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Rodriguez, whose 4.74 xERA provides a soft landing for a hitter with his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** finds himself in an ideal position; despite a solid opponent in Kolek, the elite 0.452 xwOBA profile and high-leverage order placement at #2 make him a near-automatic start for Roto production. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-first strategy with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.38), who leverages a significant +14% dynamic platoon boost and the leadoff spot to capitalize on his elite sprint speed, even against a tough arm in Webb.\n\nThe selection process was particularly tight at the fringes, with **Chase Meidroth** serving as the most notable exclusion from the starting lineup. His score of 39.35 placed him just shy of the 40.0 Zebras floor; while his underlying metrics are steady, the SP skill penalty associated with facing Sheehan proved to be the deciding factor in keeping him on the bench. We are also exercising caution regarding **Gary Sanchez** (42.46) and **Casey Schmitt** (44.48). **Gary Sanchez** is facing an elite arm in S\u00e1nchez (2.72 xERA), and while his platoon advantage at the #4 spot keeps him just above our cut-off, his ceiling is severely capped today. Likewise, **Casey Schmitt** faces a negative dynamic platoon adjustment that mitigates the benefit of his #5 order slot. Monitor the status of **Kyle Schwarber** (55.33), as his performance against Harrison will be vital to our HR and RBI goals, though his score remains tempered by the high quality of the opposing pitching staff.",
